    {
      "id": "ic-Z5OXvfmF1v-v7WcJva",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2032.473801973084,
      "y": 1197.2987948268797,
      "width": 450,
      "height": 375,
      "angle": 0,
      "autoResize": true,
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "containerId": null,
      "created": 1794642566337,
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "fontSize": 20,
      "frameId": null,
      "groupIds": [],
      "index": "aM",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "opacity": 100,
      "originalText": "RLConfig\n- serviceId\n- ruleId\n- match {method, path}\n- keyBy (userId | apiKey | ip | global)\n- capacity (burst)\n- refillPerSec\n- onFailure (local_fallback | open | closed)\n- enabled\n- updatedAt\n- version\n\nPK - serviceId + ruleId\nDefault rule per service: path '*'\n",
      "roughness": 1,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 829124125,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "text": "RLConfig\n- serviceId\n- ruleId\n- match {method, path}\n- keyBy (userId | apiKey | ip | global)\n- capacity (burst)\n- refillPerSec\n- onFailure (local_fallback | open | closed)\n- enabled\n- updatedAt\n- version\n\nPK - serviceId + ruleId\nDefault rule per service: path '*'\n",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "updated": 1794643276349,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1345138419,
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
    {
      "id": "xStV9WQL8S1R2jof5tj7_",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1052.8758029979351,
      "y": 1506.302283147552,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 675,
      "angle": 0,
      "autoResize": false,
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "containerId": null,
      "created": 1794642833469,
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "fontSize": 20,
      "frameId": null,
      "groupIds": [],
      "index": "aQ",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "opacity": 100,
      "originalText": "\n- RL lives in API Gateway as middleware; its local token batch is soft state,\nso no sticky routing is needed\n- Service owners write config to RL CP directly (authz per serviceId); gateway\nonly reads\n- Gateway polls CP snapshot with ETag every 30-60s + jitter; exponential\nbackoff on failure; keeps last-known-good config on disk\n- RL keeps a local token batch and leases the next batch from Redis when it\nruns out (never over-admits, <5ms). Batch <= 10% of capacity so tokens\nstranded on an idle or dead node stay small\n- RL service Algorithm :\n    - TokenBucket - to handle burst access + deterministic limit\n    Alternatives\n    - SlidingWindowCounter - if approximation is ok\n    - Leaky Bucket if backend needs regulated flow\n- Lazy refill on access: tokens = min(capacity, tokens + elapsed *\nrefillPerSec), done in one atomic Lua script using Redis TIME\n- Shard redis on the full bucket key (identity can be userId / ip / apiKey)\n- If redis is unavailable then as per PA, fallback to local limit, roughly\nlimit / nodeCount (from service discovery); failclose only for sensitive\nURLs like login (onFailure per rule)\n- Leasing won't work for small limits (capacity < nodeCount x min batch);\nthose are checked directly on redis\n- X-RateLimit-Remaining is best-effort under leasing (a node only knows its\nown batch)\n- Multiple rules on one request: check the most restrictive first; a token\nspent on an earlier rule is not returned",
      "roughness": 1,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 774801885,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "strokeStyle": "dotted",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "text": "\n- RL lives in API Gateway as middleware; its local token batch is soft state,\nso no sticky routing is needed\n- Service owners write config to RL CP directly (authz per serviceId); gateway\nonly reads\n- Gateway polls CP snapshot with ETag every 30-60s + jitter; exponential\nbackoff on failure; keeps last-known-good config on disk\n- RL keeps a local token batch and leases the next batch from Redis when it\nruns out (never over-admits, <5ms). Batch <= 10% of capacity so tokens\nstranded on an idle or dead node stay small\n- RL service Algorithm :\n    - TokenBucket - to handle burst access + deterministic limit\n    Alternatives\n    - SlidingWindowCounter - if approximation is ok\n    - Leaky Bucket if backend needs regulated flow\n- Lazy refill on access: tokens = min(capacity, tokens + elapsed *\nrefillPerSec), done in one atomic Lua script using Redis TIME\n- Shard redis on the full bucket key (identity can be userId / ip / apiKey)\n- If redis is unavailable then as per PA, fallback to local limit, roughly\nlimit / nodeCount (from service discovery); failclose only for sensitive\nURLs like login (onFailure per rule)\n- Leasing won't work for small limits (capacity < nodeCount x min batch);\nthose are checked directly on redis\n- X-RateLimit-Remaining is best-effort under leasing (a node only knows its\nown batch)\n- Multiple rules on one request: check the most restrictive first; a token\nspent on an earlier rule is not returned",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "updated": 1794645948615,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2099167443,
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
